{"step_index":340,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T06:56:34Z","thinking":"**Refining the Animation**\n\nI'm now focused on the map animation, specifically updating `map_animation`. I've determined that the line needs to be solid instead of dotted. Additionally, I'll swap the yellow/cyan dots with small airplane and ship icons to enhance the visualization.\n\n\n**Implementing the Icons**\n\nI've decided to move away from emojis and polygon drawing for the airplane and ship icons. It's much simpler to download and use small PNG icons with transparent backgrounds, and resize them to 30x30 pixels. I've found suitable public domain icons for both: the airplane from Wikimedia, and a ship as well! Now I'm preparing to paste them on the map.\n\n\n**Drawing the Icons**\n\nI've decided to create the airplane and ship icons using `PIL.ImageDraw`, avoiding external downloads. I've defined polygon coordinates for each icon, allowing rotation based on flight angle calculations from `dx` and `dy`. The current method of updating `map_animation.py` is `write_to_file`. The goal is to dynamically generate these icons and integrate them into the animation framework.\n\n\n**Calculating the Paths**\n\nI'm now calculating paths and icon positions. I'm using `get_xy` to convert latitude and longitude to screen coordinates. Bezier curves are used for path generation, and `draw_rotated_polygon` helps to orient the icons on the map based on the angle of movement. I'm setting start and end frames for the animation. I'm also ensuring that the correct font file is loaded.\n\n\n**Defining the Shapes**\n\nI'm now defining the shapes for the airplane and ship icons using polygon coordinates, and establishing paths for them. I have defined `airplane_poly` and `ship_poly` for the shapes, with the aim to use them later on, and also precomputed `plane_path` and `ship_path`. I'm focusing on defining the shapes that will be used to animate, incorporating Bezier curves. I'm also ensuring the paths are smooth.\n\n\n**Animating the Icons**\n\nI'm now focused on dynamically animating the ship and airplane icons, drawing trails, and positioning text labels. I've updated the code to draw solid trails for both icons, and I'm calculating the angle of movement from the previous and current positions for accurate icon rotation. The implementation uses `draw_rotated_polygon`, and also adds dynamic text to each frame.\n\n\n**Updating the Drawing**\n\nI've added the ship cabin as a white-filled polygon for a more detailed ship icon, and the city markers, labels for Washington D.C. and New Delhi. I'm focusing on making sure all shapes are rotated correctly and drawn in the correct positions, and that the text labels look nice.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import sys\nimport os\nimport math\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\n\noutput_dir = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\map_frames\"\nos.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nmap_path = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\world_map.jpg\"\n\nmap_img = Image.open(map_path).convert(\"RGBA\")\nmap_img = map_img.resize((1920, 1080))\n\ndef get_xy(lon, lat):\n    x = (lon + 180) * (1920 / 360.0)\n    y = (90 - lat) * (1080 / 180.0)\n    return x, y\n\ndef bezier(t, p0, p1, p2):\n    return (\n        (1-t)**2 * p0[0] + 2*(1-t)*t * p1[0] + t**2 * p2[0],\n        (1-t)**2 * p0[1] + 2*(1-t)*t * p1[1] + t**2 * p2[1]\n    )\n\ndef draw_rotated_polygon(draw, center, polygon, angle, fill, outline=\"black\"):\n    rotated = []\n    cos_a = math.cos(angle)\n    sin_a = math.sin(angle)\n    for px, py in polygon:\n        rx = px * cos_a - py * sin_a\n        ry = px * sin_a + py * cos_a\n        rotated.append((center[0] + rx, center[1] + ry))\n    draw.polygon(rotated, fill=fill, outline=outline)\n\ndc_pos = get_xy(-77.0369, 38.9072)\ndelhi_pos = get_xy(77.2090, 28.6139)\nctrl_pos = ((dc_pos[0] + delhi_pos[0])/2, min(dc_pos[1], delhi_pos[1]) - 300)\n\nship_start = get_xy(-74.0060, 40.7128)\nship_end = get_xy(-0.1276, 51.5074)\n\ntotal_frames = 450\nstart_f = int(sys.argv[1])\nend_f = int(sys.argv[2])\n\ntry:\n    font = ImageFont.truetype(\"arial.ttf\", 40)\nexcept:\n    font = ImageFont.load_default()\n\n# Precompute the paths to draw solid lines\nplane_path = [bezier(t/total_frames, dc_pos, ctrl_pos, delhi_pos) for t in range(total_frames+1)]\nship_path = [ (ship_start[0] + (ship_end[0]-ship_start[0])*(t/total_frames)*0.3,\n               ship_start[1] + (ship_end[1]-ship_start[1])*(t/total_frames)*0.3) for t in range(total_frames+1) ]\n\n# Airplane shape (facing right)\nairplane_poly = [\n    (20, 0),    # nose\n    (5, -5),    # body top\n    (-5, -20),  # left wing tip\n    (-2, -5),   # wing root top\n    (-15, -5),  # tail root top\n    (-20, -12), # left tail tip\n    (-16, 0),   # tail back\n    (-20, 12),  # right tail tip\n    (-15, 5),   # tail root bottom\n    (-2, 5),    # wing root bottom\n    (-5, 20),   # right wing tip\n    (5, 5)      # body bottom\n]\n\n# Ship shape (facing right)\nship_poly = [\n    (20, 0),    # bow\n    (12, -8),   # bow top\n    (-15, -8),  # stern top\n    (-20, -4),  # stern back\n    (-15, 8),   # stern bottom\n    (12, 8)     # bow bottom\n]\nship_cabin = [\n    (5, -8), (5, -18), (-8, -18), (-8, -8)\n]\n\nfor i in range(start_f, end_f + 1):\n    frame = map_img.copy()\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(frame)\n    \n    # Draw solid plane trail\n    if i > 0:\n        draw.line(plane_path[:i+1], fill=\"red\", width=6, joint=\"curve\")\n        \n    plane_pos = plane_path[i]\n    # Calculate angle for plane\n    if i > 0:\n        prev_pos = plane_path[i-1]\n        plane_angle = math.atan2(plane_pos[1] - prev_pos[1], plane_pos[0] - prev_pos[0])\n    else:\n        next_pos = plane_path[i+1]\n        plane_angle = math.atan2(next_pos[1] - plane_pos[1], next_pos[0] - plane_pos[0])\n        \n    # Draw airplane\n    draw_rotated_polygon(draw, plane_pos, airplane_poly, plane_angle, fill=\"yellow\")\n    draw.text((plane_pos[0]+25, plane_pos[1]-25), \"FLIGHT\", fill=\"yellow\", font=font)\n\n    # Draw solid ship trail\n    if i > 0:\n        draw.line(ship_path[:i+1], fill=\"blue\", width=4, joint=\"curve\")\n        \n    ship_pos = ship_path[i]\n    if i > 0:\n        prev_pos_s = ship_path[i-1]\n        ship_angle = math.atan2(ship_pos[1] - prev_pos_s[1], ship_pos[0] - prev_pos_s[0])\n    else:\n        next_pos_s = ship_path[i+1]\n        ship_angle = math.atan2(next_pos_s[1] - ship_pos[1], next_pos_s[0] - ship_pos[0])\n        \n    # Draw ship body and cabin\n    draw_rotated_polygon(draw, ship_pos, ship_poly, ship_angle, fill=\"cyan\")\n    draw_rotated_polygon(draw, ship_pos, ship_cabin, ship_angle, fill=\"white\")\n    draw.text((ship_pos[0]+25, ship_pos[1]-25), \"SHIP\", fill=\"cyan\", font=font)\n\n    # City markers\n    draw.ellipse([dc_pos[0]-8, dc_pos[1]-8, dc_pos[0]+8, dc_pos[1]+8], fill=\"white\", outline=\"black\", width=3)\n    draw.text((dc_pos[0]-50, dc_pos[1]+15), \"Washington D.C.\", fill=\"white\", font=font)\n    \n    draw.ellipse([delhi_pos[0]-8, delhi_pos[1]-8, delhi_pos[0]+8, delhi_pos[1]+8], fill=\"white\", outline=\"black\", width=3)\n    draw.text((delhi_pos[0]-20, delhi_pos[1]+15), \"New Delhi\", fill=\"white\", font=font)\n\n    filename = f\"frame_{i:03d}.png\"\n    frame.save(os.path.join(output_dir, filename))","Description":"Updating map animation script to include solid lines and actual airplane/ship icons drawn as polygons","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\map_animation.py","toolAction":"Updating the map script with solid lines, airplane polygons, and ship polygons","toolSummary":"Update Map Script"}}]}
