nts, so I can call the project complete.\n\n\n**Integrating the Titles**\n\nI've integrated the title text for each scene, ensuring it complements the visual narrative. Now, the Python script uses the frame index to select and display the appropriate title for each scene. I have also focused on the thumbs-up animation in the last scene, and confirmed it's working as expected.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Scene**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the text integration, and checking for potential edge cases. I realized the title array might exceed bounds in scene six, even though it's clamped to five. I reduced the font size to 70 pt to ensure the text fits comfortably within the frame width. I'm working to write the user's voiceover script alongside the script execution plan.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"mkdir \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\short_frames\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Creating directory for the YouTube Short frames","toolSummary":"Create frames directory"}}]}
